ed on v2.3.0. Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and should not be redeployed until it is fixed and verified. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial-failure."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying, to avoid paging on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MisC32v4YLVC4BfJuhi1Au", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is unhealthy and is no longer running anywhere. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the regions mixed. I re-ran the same rollback and it completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for checkout-api. The incident summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and the retry. The create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before anything else. It showed INC-0001 already existed, so I did not open a duplicate.\n\nStill open: v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until its failure is understood and fixed. The orchestrator partial failure during rollback also needs a follow-up.", "type": "text"}]}]}